      "title": "Thousand Spin Annealer Demo",
      "excerpt": "The review states that D-Wave's tunable transverse Ising hardware has been used for deep quantum learning protocols on more than a thousand spins.",
      "overview": "This hardware evidence supports the near-term deep-learning pathway because it does not require a universal fault-tolerant quantum computer. It is evidence for scale and suitability of special-purpose devices, not proof of general quantum advantage.",
      "evidence_type": "observational_result",
      "claim_refs": [
